{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The peoples heard, they trembled.</b> He mentioned here four portions of the nations corresponding to the four directions of the world, and they are the entirety of the inhabited world. Therefore he mentioned Philistia, Edom, Moab, and Canaan — that is, Philistia and all dwellers of the west; Edom and all dwellers of the south; Moab and all dwellers of the east; Canaan and all dwellers of the north. And the intention in his saying ״The peoples heard, they trembled״ is that all these nations and all who are after them — for they encompass all the inhabited world in the four directions of the world — were shaken by the splitting of the Sea of Reeds, and this great wonder was publicized to all." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> The dwellers of Philistia: the Philistines feared Israel because two hundred thousand of the children of Ephraim had been killed from among them, who calculated and erred and went out thirty years before the end. The chiefs of Edom feared them, lest they be bearing a grudge against them for the hatred between Esau and Jacob. The leaders of Moab — on account of the quarrel between the shepherds of Lot their father and the shepherds of Abraham our father. And the dwellers of Canaan — because they would inherit their land, for their wise men knew this by the wisdom of astrology."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:59:35.768637112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}